    "body": "Hey @offbyone 👋 \r\n\r\nIt looks like it may be a few things affecting your custom modules:\r\n1. We aren't using TOML arrays for custom modules, so you'll want to use single brackets: \r\n  `[[custom.simple]]` → `[custom.simple]`\r\n2. It seems you're using the `$value` variable instead of `$output`.\r\n3. For me, personally, `true` was located in `/usr/bin/true`, so I replaced that locally to just `true`.\r\n\r\nWith the following adjustments, I was able to get the \"simple\" custom module working locally:\r\n```diff\r\n-- [[custom.simple]]\r\n++ [custom.simple]\r\ndescription = \"simple\"\r\n-- when = \"/bin/true\"\r\n++ when = \"true\"\r\ncommand = \"echo yes\"\r\n-- format = \"[$value](fg:blue)\"\r\n++ format = \"[$output](fg:blue)\"\r\nshell = [\"bash\", \"--noprofile\", \"--norc\"]\r\n```",
